  abstract     = {In mathematics, the n-th harmonic number H_n is the sum of the reciprocals of the first n natural numbers. Harmonic numbers are closely related to the harmonic series and the Riemann zeta function, arise in many identities and applications in number theory and analysis, and have the asymptotic behavior H_n = \gamma + \ln n + o(1), where \gamma is the Euler--Mascheroni constant.},
